The diagram is a net with six equal square faces. Name the model it makes and describe how to assemble it.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=12mm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (1,1);
\draw (1,0) rectangle (2,1);
\draw (2,0) rectangle (3,1);
\draw (3,0) rectangle (4,1);
\draw (1,1) rectangle (2,2);
\draw (1,-1) rectangle (2,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The diagram shows a square with one triangle attached to each side. The triangles are identical equilateral triangles, and every triangle side matches a square side. Name the model it makes, list its faces and describe how to assemble it.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=12mm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (2,2);
\draw (0,0)--(1,-1.7320508)--(2,0);
\draw (2,0)--(3.7320508,1)--(2,2);
\draw (2,2)--(1,3.7320508)--(0,2);
\draw (0,2)--(-1.7320508,1)--(0,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

These drawings show a model resting on its base. Its side view is the same as its front view. Identify the model and describe which face pieces to use to build it.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2,0)--(1,2)--cycle;
\path (1,-0.5) node {Front view};
\draw (4,0) rectangle (6,2);
\draw (4,0)--(5,1)--(6,0);
\draw (4,2)--(5,1)--(6,2);
\path (5,-0.5) node {Top view};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
